//! Conversion tables for the Japanese normalizer, machine-derived from the
//! reference.
//!
//! DO NOT EDIT BY HAND. The derived tables (`HF_*`, [`NORMALIZE`],
//! [`FH_PUNCTUATION`]) were dumped from the running reference rather than
//! re-derived here, because its `flip()` is last-writer-wins and its `merge()`
//! preserves
//! first-insertion position — two properties a hand-written inversion silently
//! gets wrong. The most visible casualty is `-`, which flips back to U+2500 BOX
//! DRAWINGS LIGHT HORIZONTAL rather than the U+FF0D fullwidth hyphen it also came
//! from.
//!
//! Every key is BMP and at most two `char`s long, and no key is a proper prefix
//! of a later key in its table — the generator refuses to emit a table that
//! breaks either property. That is what makes the leftmost-*first* alternation
//! The reference builds exactly leftmost-*longest*, which is what [`Table`]
//! implements.

use crate::table::Table;

